#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054418 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054792 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ee8b693-8158-55a9-adcd-0ece37ad7226" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Linear Equations Without the Reciprocal"}] :question/id #uuid "2d0477ef-8561-5404-b97a-99a49031c4ef" :question/math-academy-id "e-13031" :question/problem "Solve for $x$, if $-\\dfrac{3}{4}x = 12$." :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply both sides by $\\color{blue}4$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-\\frac{3}{4}x &= 12 \\\\\n4 \\cdot (-\\frac{3}{4}x) &= 4 \\cdot 12 \\\\\n4 \\cdot (-\\frac{3}{4}x) &= 48 \\\\\n- 3x &= 48\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by ${\\color{red}-3}$ to isolate $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-3x &= 48 \\\\\n\\frac{-3x}{-3} &= \\frac{48}{-3} \\\\\n\\frac{-3x}{-3} &= -16 \\\\\nx &= -16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054419 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054793 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08568384-d6f2-503a-98f7-fa3f5052caa1" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Linear Equations With the Reciprocal"}] :question/id #uuid "9acb3bf7-12c7-51db-a8a6-30111c3b7e86" :question/math-academy-id "e-13032" :question/problem "If $-\\dfrac{3}{2}t = 24$, then what is the value of $t$?" :question/worked-solution "We multiply both sides of the equation by the reciprocal of\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nwhich is\n\n$$\n\\left(-\\dfrac{3}{2} \\right)^{-1} = -\\dfrac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-\\frac{3}{2}t &= 24 \\\\\n- \\frac{2}{3} \\cdot (-\\frac{3}{2}t) &= -\\frac{2}{3} \\cdot 24 \\\\\n1t &= -\\frac{2}{3} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 8 \\\\\nt &= -16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054420 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfc82dc4-a6bc-5677-ac4a-c1cddf29ab58" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Two-Step Linear Equations With the Reciprocal"}] :question/id #uuid "64b6a66a-c061-52e2-a3aa-e54b7542715c" :question/math-academy-id "e-13033" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\dfrac{3x}{4}-5 = -8$." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the fractional term\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3x}{4}\n$$\n\nby adding $5$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{3x}{4}-5 &=-8 \\\\[5pt] \\dfrac{3x}{4}-5+5 &=-8+5 \\\\[5pt] \\dfrac{3x}{4}+0 &=-3 \\\\[5pt] \\dfrac{3x}{4} &=-3 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe fractional coefficient is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nso we multiply by its reciprocal\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{3}{4} \\right)^{-1} = \\dfrac{4}{3}\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{3}{4}x &=-3 \\\\[5pt] \\dfrac{4}{3} \\cdot \\dfrac{3}{4}x &= \\dfrac{4}{3} \\cdot (-3) \\\\[5pt] 1 x &=-\\dfrac{4}{\\cancel{3}} \\cdot \\cancel{3} \\\\[5pt] x &= -4. \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055422 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054792 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ee8b693-8158-55a9-adcd-0ece37ad7226" :knowledge-point/title "Solving One-Step Linear Equations Without the Reciprocal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94e18e75-099e-55c2-a39c-eeb32cfe4cba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053770} {:answer/id #uuid "371b609d-3d63-5502-b962-177fef5436e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053771} {:answer/id #uuid "4f609d16-a553-51f4-b5da-88afeb95a30c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053772} {:answer/id #uuid "51123f87-4c88-57ed-91e2-cb5701fbc342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053773} {:answer/id #uuid "6d577407-a819-5ca6-9183-79b25b7e9329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\